# Flashback is an alternative cost (CR 702.34a: "by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost"), and a spell can't be
# cast for two alternative costs (CR 601.2b, 118.9a; Snapcaster Mage's ruling). Bot2's first Duress takes Force of Will from
# Bot1's hand. On turn 4 Bot2 casts a second Duress; in response Bot1 flashes in Snapcaster Mage, whose trigger gives the Force
# flashback for its mana cost. From the graveyard it may not be cast for its own alternative cost - 1 life and a blue card
# exiled, though Bot1 holds Brainstorm - but is cast for {3}{U}{U}, counters the Duress and is exiled.

